      "content": "If the premise of the struggle is fundamentally flawed—if the debt is infinite and the reward is zero—then continuing to pay is illogical. A quiet surrender isn't a failure; it's recognizing a broken system and choosing to opt out of the terms of service. It's the ultimate act of self-preservation when the whole game is rigged against you.",
